# Define the objective function: V = x(50 - 2x)(20 - 2x)
# Expand the expression: V = x(50 - 2x)(20 - 2x) = x(1000 - 140x + 4x^2) = 1000x - 140x^2 + 4x^3
# Since GLOP only supports linear objectives, we need to find the maximum of the cubic function
# by evaluating it at the critical points and endpoints

# Calculate the critical points by differentiating V and setting the derivative to zero
# V = 4x^3 - 140x^2 + 1000x
# dV/dx = 12x^2 - 280x + 1000
# Set dV/dx = 0: 12x^2 - 280x + 1000 = 0
# Solve the quadratic equation: x = [280 ± sqrt(280^2 - 4*12*1000)] / (2*12)
# Calculate the discriminant: 280^2 - 4*12*1000 = 78400 - 48000 = 30400
# sqrt(30400) = 174.3559577467857
# x = [280 ± 174.3559577467857] / 24
# x1 = (280 + 174.3559577467857) / 24 ≈ 18.9315 cm (not valid as it exceeds the width)
# x2 = (280 - 174.3559577467857) / 24 ≈ 4.4021 cm

# Evaluate the volume at the critical point x ≈ 4.4021 cm
x_critical = 4.4021
